        "body": "When meeting cadence review changes a record in the operational record, the operations lead approves and the preparer records the action; the two roles stay separate. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. Record rejected and deferred requests as well as approvals. When urgency presses against the limit, pause and route the decision. The meeting cadence review reviewer records the review note, the owner, and the next action in one place.\n\nA role change should trigger a review of queue access. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. When urgency presses against the limit, pause and route the decision. A meeting cadence review exception keeps the review note attached and routes the question to the operations lead.\n\nIf the team cannot reproduce the result from the record, the control is not finished. Write the authority limit into the case template. If two roles share a queue, mark which one decides each item. A case that moves between owners should keep both owner periods visible. For meeting cadence review, the working file keeps the meeting series list and the decision log beside the decision note."
